lesson k-drawing-what-you-see v=1 format=teach grade=0 unit=9 subject=art levels=[easy, medium, hard] {
  title "Drawing what you see"
  goal "Look for the big shapes in a thing, draw the big shape first and the small parts after, and count the shapes in a picture."

  look {
    scene 18x12 {
      collage pic scene=house at=canvas(1, 1)
    }
    say """
      This house is made of shapes: a big square, a triangle for the roof, and small rectangles for
      the door and the windows. When you draw what you see, find the big shape first, then add the
      small parts.
      """
  }
  do {
    level easy {
      worked k.shape-of-a-thing k=0 level=medium
    }
    practice k.shape-of-a-thing count=2 seed=2
    practice k.big-shape-first count=2 seed=3 easy-count=1
    practice k.shapes-in-a-picture count=3 seed=4 easy-count=2
    show k.draw-a-cup
  }
  try stars=2 {
    show k.bigger-is-nearer
  }
  try stars=3 {
    show k.all-the-shapes s="fish" easy-s="boat" hard-s="house"
  }
  remember {
    say "Look first. Draw the big shape, then the small parts."
  }

  grown-ups """
    Read each question aloud. The drawing of the cup is for you to look at: it should come from
    looking at a real cup, so put one on the table. Children draw what they know rather than what
    they see, so ask where the handle really is. If the child is stuck, trace round the cup's
    shape in the air together. Off the page, draw a toy from three sides. Japan, 幼稚園教育要領
    (kindergarten guidelines), 表現, 内容 (4): "感じたこと，考えたことなどを音や動きなどで表現したり，自由にかいたり，つくったりなどする。"
    (Express what they feel and think through sound and movement, and draw and make things freely.)
    """
  level easy {
    grown-ups "At this level the plate is shaped in the teacher's pen first, the picture to count is the boat or the fish, and the house comes second."
  }
  level hard {
    grown-ups "At this level the shapes to find are the door and the square window, the pictures to count are the fish and the house, and the three-star counts every piece of the house."
  }
}
